------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What the models are
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  * detector.onnx: a card detector derived from YOLOX. It was fine-tuned from
    the COCO-pretrained YOLOX-Nano weights published by Megvii
    (https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX, Apache-2.0).
  * recognizer.onnx: the cardvision recognizer (MobileNetV3-Small, started
    from torchvision's ImageNet-pretrained weights, BSD-3-Clause code), trained
    to output one 128-value vector per card picture.
  * bank.json: one vector per known card, computed by the recognizer from card
    art. It does not contain the art.

Both models were trained by the open-source cardvision project (toolkit release
coming; see https://github.com/ryangswe/kenbunshoku#built-on-cardvision) on
labels made on frames of public videos, plus synthetic composites made from
official card art. No card art, video frame or label is included here.
PROVENANCE.md says more.

